      "writtenOn": "2025-10-15T01:53:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Question: why exactly need to put the FPU if it is in use?\n\nIf it is in use, we need to put the fpu so that the fpu hardware state can be saved into fpstate memory, then we clear it and re-load to make sure the fpu hardware runs with the reset value.\n\n\u003e Also in what cases fpstate-\u003ein_use may be already true when kvm_vcpu_reset() is called?\n\nCurrently seems it doesn\u0027t have this case as kvm_vcpu_reset() is used via the PV interface by the host, thus fpstate in this case is not in use. But checking in_use flag is more flexible in case we will need to the pkvm hypervisor to actively do a kvm_vcpu_reset(), not sure if this will benefit to the secondary vcpu securely bringing up?.",
      "parentUuid": "9d602502_bef2585c",
      "revId": "cb6c7508841c8a33ef9006d8a21449c0272c98fc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0f33c065_c17f7f9c",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/x86.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 2919,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-15T10:37:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see. Yeah, I\u0027m ok with keeping this checking here even if it currently not used (even if just to echo the init_event checks below).\n\n\u003e not sure if this will benefit to the secondary vcpu securely bringing up?.\n\nProbably not, it will only call kvm_vcpu_reset() before a secondary vCPU runs first time, i.e. before we even enter kvm_vcpu_enter_guest() first time for the given vCPU.\n\n...Maybe let\u0027s add a comment before this check, like \"With the existing pKVM code paths, the fpstate should not be in use at this point. Still check it, in case this changes in the future.\" ?",
      "parentUuid": "0bacd708_818d20c1",
      "revId": "cb6c7508841c8a33ef9006d8a21449c0272c98fc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
